<title>USA: Pittsburgh group proposes development bond ballot.</title>
<headline>Pittsburgh group proposes development bond ballot.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Pittsburgh group is proposing a bond question for the fall ballot to boost what it sees as a dearth of development efforts in the region.</p>
<p>Regional Renaissance Partnership says money is needed because the region is lagging behind other parts of the country in job creation.</p>
<p>The group said the bonds could be used for a regional growth fund.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
